  "title": "Trump shifts to economic pressure on Iran as Strait of Hormuz remains closed",
  "summary": "Iran insists the Strait of Hormuz will remain closed until Trump agrees to its demands, while the US continues its blockade to weaken Iran's hold on the waterway. The conflict has stalled for over five months, with both sides pushing for different approaches to resolve the crisis.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Iran holds firm on the Strait of Hormuz and insists it will remain closed until Trump agrees to its demands.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The US continues its blockade of Iran's ports, with Trump dropping a 24-hour-old vow to charge cargo ships for using the Strait.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Trump's economic pressure is a key strategy to ease the conflict and ease pressure on oil prices.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
